---
import Layout from "../../Base.astro";
import SimpleHero from "../../components/SimpleHero.astro";
import FeaturedArticles from "../../components/FeaturedArticles.astro";
import ServicesRelatedWork from "../../components/ServicesRelatedWork.astro";
import "../../styles/pages/_services-list.scss";
---

<Layout
  title="Marketing Reporting &amp; Measurement | Kelp Agency"
  description="Reporting that connects campaigns and websites to qualified leads, sales, customer behavior, and the next decision."
>
  <SimpleHero
    tagline="Digital Marketing Services"
    title="Reporting"
    description="Data is not useful if your team still does not know what to do next. We build reporting that turns scattered metrics into clear decisions about budget, content, and growth."
    lottieFile="reporting.json"
  />
  <div class="service-body">
    <div class="wrapper wrapper--narrow">
      <h2>Where teams get stuck</h2>
      <p>
        Most businesses are not short on data. They are short on clarity.
        Metrics live in different platforms, dashboards answer the wrong
        questions, and reporting meetings end without a decision.
      </p>
      <p>
        That makes it hard to know what is actually working, what needs to
        change, and where the next dollar should go.
      </p>
      <h2>How we fix it</h2>
      <p>
        We start with the decisions your team needs to make, then build
        reporting around the signals that support those decisions. That can
        include campaign performance, channel trends, benchmarks over time, and
        the context needed to interpret the numbers correctly.
      </p>
      <p>
        The goal is not to hand over more charts. It is to give you a clearer
        read on what is happening and what should happen next.
      </p>
      <h2>Define the Result First</h2>
      <p>
        We agree on what counts as a useful action and how it will be recorded.
        That may mean contact forms, bookings, calls, purchases, or a later
        sales-stage outcome. Then we review the tracking, channel labels,
        landing pages, and data quality that support the report. A raw lead
        count without quality or source context can send a team in the wrong
        direction.
      </p>
      <h2>Review the Full Path</h2>
      <p>
        We look for patterns across traffic, campaigns, website behavior, and
        outcomes. The report should help decide whether to change targeting,
        copy, creative, page experience, or budget. AI referral traffic can be
        observed where platforms provide it, but a single AI answer is not a
        stable ranking. Talk with Kelp about a reporting rhythm your team can
        use.
      </p>
      <h2>How This Works in Practice</h2>
      <p>
        Different teams need different levels of detail. Leadership needs to see
        whether marketing supports the business goal; the people running
        campaigns need enough detail to make changes. We define those views
        together and note where tracking is incomplete. A useful report should
        make uncertainty clear, explain movement in context, and end with a
        short list of decisions for the next period.
      </p>
      <h2>What the Work Includes</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Measurement definitions and event review</li>
        <li>Channel and landing-page reporting</li>
        <li>Lead-quality or sales feedback loop</li>
        <li>A concise review with recommended actions</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>What Moving Forward Looks Like</h2>
      <p>
        Bring the reports you already use and a few decisions they have failed
        to answer. We can identify which data is missing, which metric is
        misleading, and what a useful reporting cadence would look like.
      </p>
      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <h3>Can you report on AI search referrals?</h3>
      <p>
        Where a referral source is identifiable, yes. We can review it alongside
        organic search and qualified outcomes, while recognizing that AI
        responses vary and attribution has limits.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="/contact/" class="button button--green">
          Make Reporting Useful
        </a>
      </p>
    </div>
    <ServicesRelatedWork tag={79} />
  </div>
  <FeaturedArticles />
</Layout>
